{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":25830260,"ns":0,"title":"Annulus theorem","extract":"In mathematics, the annulus theorem (formerly called the annulus conjecture) states roughly that the region between two well-behaved spheres is an annulus. It is closely related to the stable homeomorphism conjecture (now proved) which states that every orientation-preserving homeomorphism of Euclidean space is stable.","description":"In mathematics, on the region between two well-behaved spheres","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}